           "fact": "F5",
           "source": "lem-maximal-ode-solution-extends-from-compact-tube",
           "source_section": "Statement",
-          "quote": "Let $d\\ge1$ and $D\\subseteq\\mathbb R\\times\\mathbb R^d$ be open and let $f:D\\to\\mathbb R^d$ be continuous and locally Lipschitz in the state variable. Let $x:I\\to\\mathbb R^d$ be a maximal solution of $x'=f(t,x)$ on an interval with finite right endpoint $b$, and fix $t_0\\in I$ with $t_0<b$. Suppose there is a compact set $C\\subseteq D$ containing $(t,x(t))$ for every $t\\in[t_0,b)$. Then $x$ has a solution extension to an interval containing $b$ and points larger than $b$. The compact set hypothesis is a tube condition: it supplies both boundedness of $f$ along the graph and a limit point inside the open domain.",
