-          "quote": "Set the first proposal to $h_0=h_{\\rm init}$. At an accepted-step state $(t_n,y_n)$, choose trial size $h=\\min(h_n,h_{\\max},T-t_n)$. If $T-t_n=0$, return `success`. If $h=0$ before reaching $T$, or any stage evaluation is undefined/nonfinite, return `failure`. Compute both pair outputs. Define the component scale $s_i=\\mathrm{atol}+\\mathrm{rtol}\\max(|(y_n)_i|,|Y_i|)$ and scaled norm $Q=\\max_i |(\\widehat Y-Y)_i|/s_i$. If $Q\\le1$, accept $Y$: set $t_{n+1}=t_n+h$, $y_{n+1}=Y$. Otherwise reject and retain $(t_n,y_n)$. In either case compute the model factor\n$$g=\\begin{cases}\\gamma_{\\max},&Q=0,\\\\ \\min(\\gamma_{\\max},\\max(\\gamma_{\\min},\\sigma /\\sqrt[p+1]{Q})),&Q>0.\\end{cases}$$\nSet next proposal to $\\min(h_{\\max},\\max(h_{\\min},g h))$. If an attempted step was rejected with $h\\le h_{\\min}$ (including a final clipped step shorter than $h_{\\min}$), return `minimum-step-rejected`; if the $N$th attempt ends without reaching $T$, return `attempt-budget-exhausted`. Before an accepted step, if its remaining distance to $T$ is smaller than $h_{\\min}$, the final clipped step is permitted. For $Q>0$, $\\sqrt[p+1]{Q}$ is the unique positive $(p+1)$st root supplied by [[thm-nth-roots-exist]]. The exponent $1/(p+1)$ is a leading-error model for step selection; neither acceptance nor this controller is a global error certificate or a stiffness test.",
